			"SHA": "d0509bfd76c9f236078714086d2488def73927f7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-09T01:02:19Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				686,
				8
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement ProcessPolyfill and NativeHostService for VS Code compatibility\n\nAdd Tauri commands for Wind's ProcessPolyfill providing process.getExecPath(), process.getPlatform(), process.getArch(), process.getPid(), process.getShellEnv(), and process.getMemoryInfo() with cross-platform implementations (macOS, Windows, Linux).\n\nAdd health check commands for SharedProcessProxy: cocoon_extension_host_health, cocoon_search_service_health, cocoon_debug_service_health, and shared_process_service_health.\n\nExpand WindServiceHandlers to support VS Code's NativeHostService interface including:\n- File system operations with URI argument support (extract_path_from_arg normalizes VS Code URI objects with scheme/path/fsPath to native paths)\n- Userdata path resolution (/User/... → ~/.land/User/...) with automatic directory initialization\n- Native dialogs (pickFolderAndOpen, showOpenDialog)\n- OS properties and statistics via sysinfo crate (added as dependency)\n- Dark mode detection across macOS (AppleInterfaceStyle), Windows (AppsUseLightTheme), and Linux (gsettings)\n- PTY profile detection for terminal integration\n- Clipboard, window state, power management, and network operations\n- Storage service implementation (getItems, updateItems)\n\nUpdate Tauri capabilities to include dialog, fs, window state, and event permissions.",
			"SHA": "2abd82d845ca6d169050c7323dd096b7ce4cb9c1"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-08T16:15:05Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				684,
				1
			],
			"Message": "build(Mountain): Enable global Tauri API in webview\n\nEnable the `withGlobalTauri` option in tauri.conf.json to expose Tauri's JavaScript APIs globally in the webview context. This allows the Wind frontend to access `window.__TAURI__` and related APIs for IPC communication without explicit imports.\n\nThis change complements the recent CSP and event listening capabilities added for Mountain-Wind communication, ensuring the frontend can properly interface with the Tauri backend.",
			"SHA": "03582136dd1417717ba2aad755eaef7241ccae6a"
		},
